  "profile": "skulk.managed/1",
  "protocol": 5,
  "semantics": [
    "All nested descriptor contracts normalize through the unchanged portable profile. Duplicate identities, surfaces, credentials, exposures and dependencies refuse.",
    "Manifest identity is full domain-separated SHA-256. Startup binds that exact normalized manifest digest. Neither digest is an execution authorization.",
    "Manifest executable is a relative artifact entry without empty/dot segments, NUL or backslash. Startup executable and socket paths are absolute POSIX paths without dot segments or NUL. Host resolves and verifies the entry without rewriting the signed manifest. Runtime dependency roots exclude pip.",
    "PEP 440 compatibility syntax is validated; the host must additionally enforce its actual version, supported profiles, signature, current trust and selection.",
    "Read manifests contain only read descriptors. Steward exposure behavior agrees with its descriptor; only read/observation may be directly exposed without governance.",
    "Durable operation annotations require operation bounds. Preflight declarations require configuration schema. Surface kind rules are enforced.",
    "Startup settings obey the portable configuration schema and encoded size bound. Non-unary manifests require a stream socket. Serve hosts are unicast non-loopback IP literals.",
    "Startup records contain secrets, must travel only over protected inherited IPC, and must never be logged or published. Refusal messages contain no input data."
  ]
